    ('8d973763-2826-4160-b790-2084c33f9e34', v_uni_id, 'LANG20480', 'Russian General Purposes 4 (CEFR A2.2)', 'Centre English&Global Language', 'The objective of this module is to enable students to develop their language competence to an intermediate level. Students will learn to perform a range of language tasks in familiar and social contexts with an emphasis on strategies for communication. The skills of reading and listening comprehension will be extended and the knowledge and use of Russian grammar and syntax consolidated and extended. The module will provide the opportunity to deepen students’ understanding and appreciation of the customs, culture and society of Russian speaking regions. This module will be delivered via small group teaching with classes having a maximum of 16 students. Students will also have access to extra resources and materials via the Virtual Learning Environment, Brightspace. For more information about the Centre for English and Global Languages modules (formerly Applied Language Centre) see https://www.ucd.ie/cegl/programmes/glm/', 'https://www.ucd.ie/modules/LANG20480', 'lang20480'),
    ('546be972-cb73-4960-ac6a-3ad474442e1c', v_uni_id, 'LANG20490', 'Spanish General Purposes 7 (CEFR B2.2)', 'Centre English&Global Language', 'This module is designed for students who have a B2 level of Spanish and wish to improve their cultural and linguistic skills in a global economy. Students will improve their understanding of Spanish with the support of video. Skills will be integrated and focus on accuracy and fluency in speaking and writing and improvement of reading and listening skills. Students will have the opportunity to enhance their communication skills through the preparation of structured presentations on longer, demanding topics. Well-structured, detailed texts will be written on complex subjects. Aspects of life and culture in Spanish-speaking regions will be introduced through written and spoken texts and classroom discussions. This module will be delivered via small group teaching with classes having a maximum of 18 students. Students will also have access to extra resources and materials via the Virtual Learning Environment, Brightspace. For more information about the Centre for English and Global Languages modules (formerly Applied Language Centre) see https://www.ucd.ie/cegl/programmes/glm/', 'https://www.ucd.ie/modules/LANG20490', 'lang20490'),
    ('a0ee93bd-e7ea-4f70-b195-c8ab92fc9655', v_uni_id, 'LANG20500', 'German General Purposes 7 (CEFR B2.2)', 'Centre English&Global Language', 'This module is designed for students who have a B2.1 level of German and wish to improve their cultural and linguistic skills in a global economy. Students will improve their understanding of German with the support of video. Skills will be integrated and focus on accuracy and fluency in speaking and writing and improvement of reading and listening skills. Students will have the opportunity to enhance their communication skills through the preparation of structured presentations on longer, demanding topics. Well-structured, detailed texts will be written on complex subjects. Aspects of life and culture in German-speaking regions will be introduced through written and spoken texts and classroom discussions. This module will be delivered via small group teaching with classes having a maximum of 18 students. Students will also have access to extra resources and materials via the Virtual Learning Environment, Brightspace. For more information about Centre for English and Global Languages modules see https://www.ucd.ie/cegl/programmes/glm/', 'https://www.ucd.ie/modules/LANG20500', 'lang20500'),
    ('08cf64d4-8a5d-42f7-9f7b-e127b3833c19', v_uni_id, 'LANG20510', 'Italian General Purposes 4 (CEFR A2.2)', 'Centre English&Global Language', 'The objective of this module is to enable students to develop their language competence to an intermediate level. Students will learn to perform a range of language tasks in familiar and social contexts with an emphasis on strategies for communication. The skills of reading and listening comprehension will be extended and the knowledge and use of Italian grammar and syntax consolidated and extended. The module will provide the opportunity to deepen students’ understanding and appreciation of the customs, culture and society of Italian speaking regions. This module will be delivered via small group teaching with classes having a maximum of 18 students. Students will also have access to extra resources and materials via the Virtual Learning Environment, Brightspace. For more information about Centre for English and Global Languages modules see https://www.ucd.ie/cegl/programmes/glm/', 'https://www.ucd.ie/modules/LANG20510', 'lang20510'),
